| `N ≡ 1 (8)`: `(2/p) = (2/q)` and the `2^5` bit = [2 is a square mod N] | `N ≡ 1 (mod 8)` | 442 | 3 418 | 0 |
| **4-rank criterion** (`Cl(−8N)` if `ε=+1`, `Cl(−4N)` if `ε=−1`) | `N ≡ 1 (mod 8)` | 442 | 3 418 | 0 |
| extra: mod-64 formula, `N ≡ 5 (8)` | `N ≡ 5 (mod 8)` | 460 | 3 483 | 0 |
